WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.450
Lean on a heavy crate
with a push of 10 newtons.

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.010
It doesn't budge.

3
00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.550
Friction pushes back
with exactly 10 newtons.

4
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.380
Push with 30 newtons.

5
00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:11.740
Still nothing.

6
00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.060
Friction rises to match you.

7
00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:17.830
It looks as if friction always
fights the way things move.

8
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.460
Can friction ever push an object forwards,

9
00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:23.250
in the direction it is already moving?

10
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.330
In this mission, you'll pin down
which way friction really acts,

11
00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:30.290
starting with a box
riding on a moving belt.

12
00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:35.450
Then you'll untangle a trickier case: a
block sliding on a board that is itself

13
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.090
being pulled along.

14
00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:41.520
Your mission: find out whether friction
can ever push an object forwards,

15
00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:42.760
and explain when.
